 widely used among developers working in that application area.

 The "System Libraries" of an executable work include anything, other
 than the work as a whole, that (a) is included in the normal form of
 packaging a work with other non-essential parts, and (b) serves only
 to enable the work to operate with a major component of the system
 in a specific manner.  A "Companion Format" of an object code work
 means an object code work minus its System Libraries.

 "Corresponding Source" for an object code work means all the source
 code needed to generate, install, and (for executable work) run the
 object code and to modify the work, including scripts to control
 those activities.  However, it does not include the work's System
 Libraries, or general-purpose tools or generally available free
 programs which are used unmodified in performing those activities but
 which do not become part of the work.  For example, Corresponding
 Source includes interface definition files associated with source
