===============================================================================
                        5E.TOOLS SPECIFIC ATTRIBUTION
===============================================================================

The following data files from the 5etools-mirror-3/5etools-src repository are used by this project
(for local import into the SQLite database at build/runtime):

- data/classfeatures.json — Class feature definitions with entries
- data/subclassfeatures.json — Subclass feature definitions with entries
- data/optionalfeatures.json — Optional class features (Metamagic, Fighting Styles, etc.)
- data/spells.json — Spell definitions
- data/feats.json — Feat definitions
- data/items.json — Magic items and equipment
- data/classes.json — Class definitions (hit die, spellcasting, levels, subclasses)
- data/backgrounds.json — Background definitions
- data/races.json — Species/race definitions
- data/conditionsdiseases.json — Conditions and diseases
- data/tables.json — Roll tables

This project does NOT redistribute the 5etools-src data files directly. They are
expected to be present locally at ../5etools-src/data/ relative to the server
binary, or the import step is skipped with a warning. The database stores only
the imported feature descriptions and metadata necessary for the character builder
to function.

If you are a 5e.tools maintainer and have concerns about this usage, please
contact the project author at andre_ataide@proton.me.

